{% comment %}
  Header Menu Bar
  File: snippets/header-menu.liquid

  Renders the desktop nav bar (.menu-bar), built from this section's
  blocks (single-link, link-list, mega-menu, highlight, flyout, @app).
  Hidden below 1024px via CSS — mobile/tablet use the separate drawer
  in snippets/header-hamburger.liquid instead.

  Loads its own CSS (header-menu.css) plus the CSS/JS for each block
  type that can appear in this bar (link-list, mega-menu, flyout-menu),
  since none of those assets are used anywhere else in the header. This
  means sections/main-header.liquid doesn't need to know any of these
  assets exist.

  Params:
    blocks — section.blocks from sections/main-header.liquid

  UPDATED: mega-menu panels used to render inside their trigger's <li>,
  i.e. as descendants of .menu-bar__list. .menu-bar__list needs
  overflow-x: auto for horizontal scroll on crowded nav bars, and per
  the CSS spec that forces overflow-y to compute as auto too — which
  silently clipped the dropdown panel sitting below it. A prior fix
  toggled the list to overflow: visible while a panel was open, but
  overflow-x/overflow-y are coupled: forcing one axis to visible forces
  the other to visible as well, so that also un-clipped the horizontal
  scroll, revealing every overflowed nav item at once.
  Fixed properly here: mega-menu panels now render AFTER </ul>, as
  siblings of .menu-bar__list rather than descendants of it (still
  inside .menu-bar__container, which is what the panel positions itself
  against — see mega-menu.css). .menu-bar__list's overflow/mask never
  need to change state now, since the panel was never really "inside"
  the thing that scrolls. Each panel is matched back to its trigger via
  a shared data-mega-index (see snippets/mega-menu.liquid and
  assets/mega-menu.css), not DOM nesting.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'header-menu.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'highlight.css'   | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'link-list.css'   | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'mega-menu.css'   | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'flyout-menu.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- if blocks.size > 0 -%}
  <nav class="menu-bar" id="main-header-menu-bar" aria-label="Primary navigation">
    <div class="menu-bar__container page-width--header">
      <ul class="menu-bar__list">
        {%- for block in blocks -%}
          {%- case block.type -%}
            {%- when 'single-link' -%}
              {%- render 'single-link', block: block -%}

            {%- when 'link-list' -%}
              {%- render 'link-list', block: block -%}

            {%- when 'mega-menu' -%}
              {%- render 'mega-menu', block: block, mode: 'trigger', mega_index: forloop.index -%}

            {%- when 'highlight' -%}
              {%- render 'highlight', block: block -%}

            {%- when 'flyout' -%}
              {%- render 'flyout-menu', block: block -%}

          {%- endcase -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>

      {%- comment -%}
        Mega-menu panels, rendered as siblings of .menu-bar__list — see
        the UPDATED note above. data-mega-index is the block's position
        in `blocks`, which is identical in both loops since we iterate
        the same collection each time (forloop.index still increments
        for skipped blocks even when the {% if %} guard below skips
        rendering them, so the numbering stays in sync with the trigger
        loop above without needing a separate counter).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- for block in blocks -%}
        {%- if block.type == 'mega-menu' -%}
          {%- render 'mega-menu', block: block, mode: 'panel', mega_index: forloop.index -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </nav>
{%- endif -%}

{{- 'link-list.js'   | asset_url | script_tag }}
{{- 'mega-menu.js'   | asset_url | script_tag }}
{{- 'flyout-menu.js' | asset_url | script_tag }}